IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2032: automated data processing and information retrieval systems.
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Same reading of results as snap4-s2020-a-d.l4: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Dates of the Act are `Date day month year`. A period of months is counted with the daydate library's `add months`.
-- The Secretary's standards, and the period the Secretary finds reasonable, are not in the sources: they are inputs.

§ `s 2032(a) Standards and procedures for reviews`

-- src:2955 | Not later than 1 year after November 28, 1990, the Secretary shall complete a review of regulations and standards (in effect on November 28, 1990) for the approval of an automated data processing and information retrieval system maintained by a State (hereinafter in this section referred to as a “system”) to determine the extent to which the regulations and standards contribute to a more effective and efficient program.
-- jural: State agencies | the Secretary | claim and duty (inferred: the text names the Secretary's duty and its object, not who may enforce it): complete the review by the deadline
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(A) (src:2955)
GIVEN `the day the Secretary completed the review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 28 November 1991, FALSE on 29 November 1991. A spent deadline, encoded because the text states it.
`s 2032(a)(1)(A) the review was completed by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the Secretary completed the review` AT MOST (`add months` (Date 28 11 1990) 12)

-- inert: 2956-2957 | reason 2 | (a)(1)(B) "The Secretary shall revise regulations (in effect on November 28, 1990) to take into account the findings of the review": a duty to revise regulations; the revised regulations are not in the Act

-- src:2959 | The regulations shall require States to incorporate all or part of systems in use elsewhere, unless a State documents that the design and operation of an alternative system would be less costly. The Secretary shall establish standards to define the extent of modification of the systems for which payments will be made under either section 2025(a) or 2025(g) of this title.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State | claim and duty: the regulations require the State to incorporate systems in use elsewhere, unless it documents that an alternative would be less costly
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(C) (src:2959)
GIVEN `the State documents that the design and operation of an alternative system would be less costly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(1)(C) the regulations must require the State to incorporate all or part of systems in use elsewhere` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State documents that the design and operation of an alternative system would be less costly`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a State documents that the design and operation of an alternative system would be less costly"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2959 | The Secretary shall establish standards to define the extent of modification of the systems for which payments will be made under either section 2025(a) or 2025(g) of this title.
-- jural: a State | the Secretary | power and liability: the Secretary's standards define how far modification of a system is paid for
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(C) (src:2959)
GIVEN `the modification is within the extent that the Secretary's standards define` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(1)(C) payments will be made under section 2025(a) or 2025(g) for the modification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the modification is within the extent that the Secretary's standards define` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the extent is defined by the Secretary's standards, which are not in these sources, and the text does not say what is paid beyond it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2961 | Proposed systems shall meet standards established by the Secretary for timely implementation of proper changes.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State proposing a system | power and liability: a proposed system must meet the Secretary's standards for timely implementation of proper changes
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(D) (src:2961)
GIVEN `the system is a proposed system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(1)(D) the system must meet the Secretary's standards for timely implementation of proper changes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system is a proposed system` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proposed systems"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2032(a)(1)(E) criterion for approval` IS ONE OF
    `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the cost effectiveness of the proposed system`
    `s 2032(a)(1)(E) any other criterion`

-- src:2963 | Criteria for the approval of a system under section 2025(g) of this title shall include the cost effectiveness of the proposed system. On implementation of the approved system, a State shall document the actual cost and benefits of the system.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State | power and liability: approval under section 2025(g) turns on criteria that include cost effectiveness
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(E) (src:2963)
GIVEN `the criterion` IS A `s 2032(a)(1)(E) criterion for approval`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(1)(E) the criteria for the approval of a system under section 2025(g) must include the criterion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the criterion`
    WHEN `s 2032(a)(1)(E) any other criterion` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall include the cost effectiveness of the proposed system"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2963 | On implementation of the approved system, a State shall document the actual cost and benefits of the system.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State | claim and duty (inferred: the text states the State's duty, not who may enforce it): document the actual cost and benefits on implementation
@ref s 2032(a)(1)(E) (src:2963)
GIVEN `the approved system has been implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(1)(E) the State must document the actual cost and benefits of the system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the approved system has been implemented` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On implementation of the approved system"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2032(a)(2) purpose of an operational review` IS ONE OF
    `s 2032(a)(2)(A) systems comply with conditions of initial funding approvals`
    `s 2032(a)(2)(B) systems adequately support program delivery in compliance with this chapter and regulations issued under this chapter`
    `s 2032(a)(2) some other purpose`

-- src:2965 | The Secretary shall conduct such reviews as are necessary to ensure that systems—
-- src:2966 | (A) comply with conditions of initial funding approvals; and
-- src:2967 | (B) adequately support program delivery in compliance with this chapter and regulations issued under this chapter.
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agencies that maintain systems | power and liability: reviews as are necessary to ensure compliance with the funding conditions and adequate support of program delivery
@ref s 2032(a)(2) (src:2965-2967)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 2032(a)(2) purpose of an operational review`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(a)(2) the Secretary must conduct the review to ensure the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `s 2032(a)(2) some other purpose` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists two purposes and does not say they are the only ones
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 2032(b) Standards for approval of systems`

-- inert: 2969-2970 | reason 2 | (b)(1) "After conducting the review required under subsection (a), the Secretary shall establish standards for approval of systems": a duty to establish standards; the standards are not in the Act

-- src:2972 | A State shall implement the standards established by the Secretary within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State | power and liability: the State must implement the standards within the reasonable period the Secretary determines
@ref s 2032(b)(2) (src:2972)
GIVEN `the period the Secretary has determined to be reasonable, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the days the State took to implement the standards` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test, counted from the day the Secretary's period begins: TRUE at the last day of the period, FALSE one day later. The length of the period is the Secretary's to determine, so it is an input.
`s 2032(b)(2) the State implemented the standards within the period the Secretary determined` MEANS
    `the days the State took to implement the standards` AT MOST `the period the Secretary has determined to be reasonable, in days`

-- src:2974 | The Secretary shall conduct appropriate periodic reviews of systems to ensure compliance with the standards established by the Secretary.
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agencies that maintain systems | power and liability: appropriate periodic reviews to ensure compliance with the standards
@ref s 2032(b)(3) (src:2974)
GIVEN `the review is a periodic review of systems to ensure compliance with the standards established by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(b)(3) the Secretary must conduct the review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the review is a periodic review of systems to ensure compliance with the standards established by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appropriate periodic reviews of systems to ensure compliance with the standards established by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2032(c) Report`

-- src:2976 | Not later than October 1, 1993, the Secretary shall report to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate on the extent to which State agencies have developed and are operating effective systems that support supplemental nutrition assistance program delivery in compliance with this chapter and regulations issued under this chapter.
-- jural: the Committees on Agriculture | the Secretary | claim and duty (inferred: the text names the Secretary's duty and the recipients of the report): report by 1 October 1993
@ref s 2032(c) (src:2976)
GIVEN `the day the Secretary reported to the Committees` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 1 October 1993, FALSE on 2 October 1993. A spent deadline, encoded because the text states it.
`s 2032(c) the report was made by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the Secretary reported to the Committees` AT MOST (Date 1 10 1993)

-- src:2976 | on the extent to which State agencies have developed and are operating effective systems that support supplemental nutrition assistance program delivery in compliance with this chapter and regulations issued under this chapter.
@ref s 2032(c) (src:2976)
GIVEN `the report is on the extent to which State agencies have developed and are operating effective systems that support program delivery in compliance with this chapter and its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2032(c) the report is the report the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report is on the extent to which State agencies have developed and are operating effective systems that support program delivery in compliance with this chapter and its regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the extent to which State agencies have developed and are operating effective systems"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
